<title>LEBANON: Saudi airlines resume Beirut flights.</title>
<headline>Saudi airlines resume Beirut flights.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-02-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Arabian Airlines resumed flights to Beirut on Saturday after a halt of nearly 15 years due to Lebanon's 1975-1990 civil war.</p>
<p>Saudi Ambassador to Beirut Ahmed al-Kohaimi, who arrived on an Airbus 300 plane, told reporters at Beirut airport that the move &quot;expressed Saudi faith in the return of security and stability to Lebanon&quot;.</p>
<p>Saudi will fly in four times every week from the main cities of Riyadh and Jeddah.</p>
</text>
